.TH "ROARK\-METRIC\-VARIANT\-UPDATE" "1" "" "roark-metric-variant-update" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-metric\-variant\-update \- Update a metric variant
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark metric variant update
\fIid\-or\-slug\fR \fIvariant\-id\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Rename a variant, change its configuration, or both. Every configuration change creates a new immutable version and advances `versionId`; the response carries the advanced value. **Editing one of Roark’s own variants forks it for your organization.** The response carries the new variant’s `id`, which will differ from the one in the path, and `isSystem` becomes false. Roark’s variant is untouched and other organizations keep it. DELETE your fork to go back to it. Which fields are editable depends on the metric: some Roark metrics lock their prompt or output configuration, and a locked field is rejected rather than ignored.
.SH "API"
PUT /v1/metric/definitions/{idOrSlug}/variants/{variantId}
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fIid\-or\-slug\fR
Metric definition UUID or its stable slug.
.TP
\fIvariant\-id\fR
Variant UUID.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<value>\fR
Rename the variant. Does not change its configuration, so `versionId` is unaffected. `Default` is reserved. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-llm\-prompt\fR \fI<value>\fR
The rubric this variant applies. LLM judge metrics only. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-scale\-min\fR \fI<value>\fR
Scale minimum. SCALE output only. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-scale\-max\fR \fI<value>\fR
Scale maximum. SCALE output only. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-boolean\-true\-label\fR \fI<value>\fR
What a `true` value means. Given to the judge as its polarity rule, so keep it accurate. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-boolean\-false\-label\fR \fI<value>\fR
What a `false` value means. Given to the judge as its polarity rule, so keep it accurate. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-classifications\fR \fI<value>\fR
Maximum classifications returned. CLASSIFICATION output only. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-change\-reason\fR \fI<value>\fR
Free\-text audit note recorded on the new version. Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt; fail instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<token>\fR
Bearer token. Prefer ROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN or the stored credential.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, plain.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Shorthand for \-\-format json.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colour.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential output.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-project\-base\-url\fR
Send the stored credential to a base URL set by a project .roark.json. Refused by default.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
roark metric variant update <id\-or\-slug> <variant\-id>
.fi
.RE
